---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="MBBS in Nepal — Frequently Asked Questions 2025 | NepalMBBS.in"
  description="Answers to the questions Indian students and parents ask most about MBBS in Nepal: NMC recognition, fees, NEET, FMGE, hostels and safety."
  path="/faq"
>
<div class="tab-pane on" id="pane-faq">
<div class="container">
  <div class="tc rev"><div class="eyebrow">Common Questions</div><div class="sec-title">Parents & Students — Top Questions</div></div>
  <div class="faq-wrap" id="faq-container">
    <div class="faq-cat">Admission & Eligibility</div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>Is NEET mandatory for Nepal MBBS?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>Yes. Per NMC India FMGL Regulations 2021, NEET is mandatory for Indian students who wish to practice medicine in India after MBBS abroad. Minimum 50th percentile for General/OBC; 40th percentile for SC/ST. Verify at <a href="https://nmc.org.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nmc.org.in</a></p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>Is a Nepal MBBS degree valid in India?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>Valid only from NMC India recognised colleges. After graduating, you must clear NExT or FMGE (conducted by NBE) + complete 1-year supervised internship in India to obtain a licence to practice. Always verify your college at <a href="https://nmc.org.in/information-desk/college-and-course-search/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NMC College Search</a> before applying.</p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>How long is the MBBS course in Nepal?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>5.5 years total — 4.5 years academic study + 1 year compulsory internship at affiliated teaching hospital. Same structure as MBBS in India. Confirmed by Nepal Medical Council official notice (November 2024).</p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>When do Nepal MBBS admissions open in 2025?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>Typically July to October. MEC Nepal publishes official admission notices at <a href="https://entrance.mec.gov.np" target="_blank" rel="noopener">entrance.mec.gov.np</a>. Apply as soon as NEET results are declared to avoid missing deadlines.</p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>How do I verify if a Nepal college is NMC India recognised?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>Search the specific college at <a href="https://nmc.org.in/information-desk/college-and-course-search/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NMC India College Search</a>. This is the ONLY authoritative source. Do not rely on college claims or agent assurances — always verify yourself.</p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-cat">Fees & Finance</div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>What is the fee for Nepal MBBS?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>Fees are regulated by MEC Nepal's official fee ceiling and vary by college. We share current official MEC fee structures during counseling — not estimates. Verify at <a href="https://mec.gov.np/en/feeStructure" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mec.gov.np/fees</a>. Always pay fees ONLY directly to the college — never to agents.</p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>Can I get an education loan for Nepal MBBS?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>Indian banks including SBI and Bank of Baroda provide education loans for MBBS at NMC India recognised foreign colleges. The college's NMC recognition letter is typically required. Consult your bank directly — terms and eligibility vary.</p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-cat">Career & Future</div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>What is NExT / FMGE and is it difficult?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>NExT (National Exit Test) is replacing FMGE for all medical graduates. Conducted by NBE twice yearly. Nepal's India-aligned curriculum provides a good foundation, but serious and dedicated preparation is required. Current info: <a href="https://natboard.edu.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">natboard.edu.in</a></p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>What internships are required after Nepal MBBS?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>Two internships required: 1) <strong>1 year in Nepal</strong> at affiliated teaching hospital during MBBS (Nepal NMC requirement, counted in the 5.5 years). 2) Additional <strong>1 year supervised internship in India</strong> after graduation (NMC India FMGL Regulations 2021). Both are mandatory to practice in India.</p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>Can I do NEET PG after Nepal MBBS?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>After clearing NExT/FMGE + completing 1-year supervised India internship, you may be eligible for NEET PG. Rules are subject to NMC updates. Always verify current eligibility at <a href="https://nmc.org.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nmc.org.in</a> before making decisions.</p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-cat">Life & Safety</div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>Do Indian students need a visa for Nepal?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>No. Indian citizens do not require a visa for Nepal under the India-Nepal bilateral open border agreement. A valid Indian passport or any government-issued photo ID is sufficient for entry into Nepal.</p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>Is Nepal safe for Indian students?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>Nepal and India share historically close cultural, diplomatic and economic ties. Indian students are generally well-received. Top medical colleges provide on-campus security and separate hostels for male and female students. We strongly recommend speaking directly with current Indian students at your shortlisted college before finalising your decision.</p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>What is the monthly living cost in Nepal?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>Approximately ₹15,000–25,000 per month covering hostel, food, transport, and personal expenses. This varies by college location, lifestyle, and individual spending. On-campus hostel living is typically the most affordable option.</p></div></div>
    <div class="faq-item rev"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><span>What documents do I need to apply?</span><div class="faq-icon">+</div></div><div class="faq-body"><p>Required: 10th+12th marksheets (notarised), NEET scorecard, valid passport, medical fitness certificate, character certificate from school/college, passport-size photos. Apply via <a href="https://entrance.mec.gov.np" target="_blank" rel="noopener">entrance.mec.gov.np</a>.</p></div></div>
  </div>
</div>
</div>
</BaseLayout>
